    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nFail the existing linting job when a Python file under `megatron/core` imports `megatron.training` or one of its submodules. Run Ruff's `TID251` rule over the entire core tree after installing the existing linting tools, emitting GitHub file/line annotations. Declare the `megatron` namespace package so relative imports are also checked, and ignore `noqa` suppressions for this check.\n\nThis adds no dependencies and leaves the existing formatting checks unchanged. Runtime imports through `importlib` are outside this static check's coverage.\n\n## Existing violations\n\n**This draft is expected to fail the new lint step until the existing violations are removed.** On the current `main` baseline, Ruff reports four imports in `megatron/core/inference/text_generation_server/dynamic_text_gen_server/vlm_dynamic_inference.py`, lines 23–26: `get_args`, `get_model`, `print_rank_0`, and the checkpoint-loading helpers. This PR adds enforcement only; it does not exempt or refactor those imports.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Executed the command parsed from the workflow with locked Ruff 0.9.10: exit 1 and exactly four expected GitHub error annotations for the existing violations.\n- Passed 18 temporary positive/negative fixtures covering absolute and relative imports, aliases, submodules, multiline imports, function-local and conditional imports, type-checking imports, suppressed imports, allowed core imports, similar module names, comments, and strings.\n- Workflow YAML parsing and shell syntax checks passed.\n- Actionlint v1.7.7 found no new diagnostics; the same two existing `needs.pre-flight` errors occur on `main`.\n- `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` passed (no changed Python files).\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
